IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`

-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), Part V -- CANCELLATION OF A BENEFIT (regulation 46.2).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: the Regulations text file, lines 474 to 480.
--
-- A beneficiary may ask in writing to cancel a benefit within 12 months of the day payment began (46.2(1)).
-- Three special routes follow for a person who gets a retirement pension and is then found to have been disabled
-- before it began: the disability application is itself deemed a request to cancel the retirement pension (2);
-- a person applying for a comparable provincial benefit has until 90 days after being told of the decision (2.1);
-- a person who gets the disability pension may undo it and have the retirement pension back within 60 days (2.2).
-- The Minister must grant a request made in any of these ways (3). If the request is granted, the amount described in
-- section 66.1(2) of the Act is repayable until the end of the 12th month after the month of granting (4).
--
-- Each period is counted from the day named: "within N days after the day on which" ends N days after that day, inclusive;
-- "12 months after" a date is the same day a year on, by the calendar rules of the core (cpp-core-calendar.l4).

§ `Part V -- Cancellation of a benefit (regulation 46.2)`

§§ `46.2(1) -- a request within 12 months of the commencement of payment`

-- src:475 | 46.2 (1) A beneficiary may submit to the Minister, within the interval between the date of commencement of payment of the benefit and the expiration of 12 months after that date, a request in writing that the benefit be cancelled.
@ref Reg 46.2(1) (src:475)
GIVEN `the date of commencement of payment of the benefit` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 46.2(1) — the last day to ask for the cancellation of a benefit` `the date of commencement of payment of the benefit` MEANS
    `the date a time limit ends` `the date of commencement of payment of the benefit` (`a number of months` WITH `number of months` IS 12)

@ref Reg 46.2(1) (src:475)
GIVEN `the date of commencement of payment of the benefit` IS A DATE
      `the date of the request` IS A DATE
      `the request is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 46.2(1) — a beneficiary's request that a benefit be cancelled is made in time and in writing`
    `the date of commencement of payment of the benefit` `the date of the request` `the request is in writing` MEANS
    `the request is in writing`
        AND `the date of the request` AT LEAST `the date of commencement of payment of the benefit`
        AND `the date of the request` AT MOST (`reg 46.2(1) — the last day to ask for the cancellation of a benefit` `the date of commencement of payment of the benefit`)

§§ `46.2(2) -- a disability application that is deemed a request to cancel the retirement pension`

-- src:476 | (2) If an applicant for a disability pension is in receipt of a retirement pension and they are deemed to have become disabled for the purpose of entitlement to the disability pension before the month in which the retirement pension became payable, the application for the disability pension is deemed to be a request for the cancellation of the retirement pension.
@ref Reg 46.2(2) (src:476)
GIVEN `the applicant for a disability pension is in receipt of a retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a day in the month in which the applicant is deemed to have become disabled for the purpose of entitlement to the disability pension` IS A DATE   -- out of range: section 42(2) (piece cp3)
      `a day in the month in which the retirement pension became payable` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 46.2(2) — the application for a disability pension is deemed to be a request for the cancellation of the retirement pension`
    `the applicant for a disability pension is in receipt of a retirement pension`
    `a day in the month in which the applicant is deemed to have become disabled for the purpose of entitlement to the disability pension`
    `a day in the month in which the retirement pension became payable` MEANS
    `the applicant for a disability pension is in receipt of a retirement pension`
        AND `the month of a date` `a day in the month in which the applicant is deemed to have become disabled for the purpose of entitlement to the disability pension`
            LESS THAN (`the month of a date` `a day in the month in which the retirement pension became payable`)

§§ `46.2(2.1) -- a comparable benefit under a provincial pension plan`

-- src:477 | (2.1) Despite subsection (1), if an applicant for a benefit under a provincial pension plan that is comparable to a disability pension is in receipt of a retirement pension and they are deemed to have become disabled for the purpose of entitlement to the benefit before the month in which the retirement pension became payable, the applicant may request cancellation of the retirement pension by submitting a written request to the Minister within the period beginning on the day of commencement of payment of the retirement pension and ending 90 days after the day on which the applicant receives notice of the decision deeming them to be disabled.
@ref Reg 46.2(2.1) (src:477)
GIVEN `the date the applicant receives notice of the decision deeming them to be disabled` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 46.2(2.1) — the last day to ask for the cancellation of the retirement pension` `the date the applicant receives notice of the decision deeming them to be disabled` MEANS
    `the date a time limit ends` `the date the applicant receives notice of the decision deeming them to be disabled` (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 90)

@ref Reg 46.2(2.1) (src:477)
GIVEN `the applicant for a benefit under a provincial pension plan that is comparable to a disability pension is in receipt of a retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a day in the month in which the applicant is deemed to have become disabled for the purpose of entitlement to the benefit` IS A DATE   -- out of range: section 42(2) (piece cp3) and the provincial plan
      `a day in the month in which the retirement pension became payable` IS A DATE
      `the day of commencement of payment of the retirement pension` IS A DATE
      `the date the applicant receives notice of the decision deeming them to be disabled` IS A DATE
      `the date of the written request` IS A DATE
      `the request is in writing to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 46.2(2.1) — an applicant for a comparable provincial benefit may request the cancellation of the retirement pension`
    `the applicant for a benefit under a provincial pension plan that is comparable to a disability pension is in receipt of a retirement pension`
    `a day in the month in which the applicant is deemed to have become disabled for the purpose of entitlement to the benefit`
    `a day in the month in which the retirement pension became payable`
    `the day of commencement of payment of the retirement pension`
    `the date the applicant receives notice of the decision deeming them to be disabled`
    `the date of the written request`
    `the request is in writing to the Minister` MEANS
    `the applicant for a benefit under a provincial pension plan that is comparable to a disability pension is in receipt of a retirement pension`
        AND `the month of a date` `a day in the month in which the applicant is deemed to have become disabled for the purpose of entitlement to the benefit`
            LESS THAN (`the month of a date` `a day in the month in which the retirement pension became payable`)
        AND `the request is in writing to the Minister`
        AND `the date of the written request` AT LEAST `the day of commencement of payment of the retirement pension`
        AND `the date of the written request` AT MOST
            (`reg 46.2(2.1) — the last day to ask for the cancellation of the retirement pension` `the date the applicant receives notice of the decision deeming them to be disabled`)

§§ `46.2(2.2) -- cancelling the disability pension and reinstating the retirement pension`

-- src:478 | (2.2) An applicant referred to in subsection (2) may request cancellation of the disability pension and reinstatement of the retirement pension by submitting a written request to the Minister within 60 days after receipt of notice of their entitlement to the disability pension.
@ref Reg 46.2(2.2) (src:478)
GIVEN `the date the applicant receives notice of their entitlement to the disability pension` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 46.2(2.2) — the last day to ask for the cancellation of the disability pension` `the date the applicant receives notice of their entitlement to the disability pension` MEANS
    `the date a time limit ends` `the date the applicant receives notice of their entitlement to the disability pension` (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 60)

@ref Reg 46.2(2.2) (src:478)
GIVEN `the applicant is an applicant referred to in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the applicant receives notice of their entitlement to the disability pension` IS A DATE
      `the date of the written request` IS A DATE
      `the request is in writing to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 46.2(2.2) — an applicant may request the cancellation of the disability pension and the reinstatement of the retirement pension`
    `the applicant is an applicant referred to in subsection (2)`
    `the date the applicant receives notice of their entitlement to the disability pension`
    `the date of the written request`
    `the request is in writing to the Minister` MEANS
    `the applicant is an applicant referred to in subsection (2)`
        AND `the request is in writing to the Minister`
        AND `the date of the written request` AT LEAST `the date the applicant receives notice of their entitlement to the disability pension`
        AND `the date of the written request` AT MOST
            (`reg 46.2(2.2) — the last day to ask for the cancellation of the disability pension` `the date the applicant receives notice of their entitlement to the disability pension`)

§§ `46.2(3) -- the Minister must grant the request`

-- src:479 | (3) The Minister shall grant a request submitted in accordance with subsection (1), (2.1) or (2.2) or deemed to be made under subsection (2).
@ref Reg 46.2(3) (src:479)
GIVEN `the request is submitted in accordance with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is submitted in accordance with subsection (2.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is submitted in accordance with subsection (2.2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is deemed to be made under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 46.2(3) — the Minister must grant the request`
    `the request is submitted in accordance with subsection (1)`
    `the request is submitted in accordance with subsection (2.1)`
    `the request is submitted in accordance with subsection (2.2)`
    `the request is deemed to be made under subsection (2)` MEANS
    `the request is submitted in accordance with subsection (1)`
        OR `the request is submitted in accordance with subsection (2.1)`
        OR `the request is submitted in accordance with subsection (2.2)`
        OR `the request is deemed to be made under subsection (2)`

§§ `46.2(4) -- repaying the amount described in subsection 66.1(2) of the Act`

-- The time begins on the granting of the request and ends on the expiration of 12 months following the month in
-- which it is granted: the last day of the 12th month after the month of granting (fork F-46.2).
-- src:480 | (4) If a request referred to in subsection 66.1(2) of the Act is granted under this section, the amount described in that subsection shall be repayable within the time beginning on the granting of the request and ending on the expiration of 12 months following the month in which the request is granted.
@ref Reg 46.2(4) (src:480)
GIVEN `the date the request is granted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 46.2(4) — the last day to repay the amount described in subsection 66.1(2) of the Act` `the date the request is granted` MEANS
    `the month following the month of a date` (`add months` (`the month of a date` `the date the request is granted`) 12) PLUS (0 MINUS 1)

@ref Reg 46.2(4) (src:480)
GIVEN `a request referred to in subsection 66.1(2) of the Act is granted under this section` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 66.1(2) (piece cp4)
      `the date the request is granted` IS A DATE
      `the date of the repayment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 46.2(4) — a repayment is made within the time the regulation allows`
    `a request referred to in subsection 66.1(2) of the Act is granted under this section`
    `the date the request is granted`
    `the date of the repayment` MEANS
    `a request referred to in subsection 66.1(2) of the Act is granted under this section`
        AND `the date of the repayment` AT LEAST `the date the request is granted`
        AND `the date of the repayment` AT MOST (`reg 46.2(4) — the last day to repay the amount described in subsection 66.1(2) of the Act` `the date the request is granted`)
